## Max's workflow on this machine

- Max decides; agents never push. Commit locally with a public-fit message (the repository boundary hook
  checks it; never bypass it). One chat writes to this working tree at a time.
- A parallel fix chat works in its own lane clone under `~/workDirectory/Critical/<project>/lanes/<id>/`
  (global rules). This project keeps the nested layout, so `projectctl` does not manage it; lanes are made
  by hand (clone of this repository, `internal/` cloned inside and excluded, boundary hooks installed,
  copies of this file and `AGENTS.md`, a `workspace.json` and a `START-HERE.md`). Max integrates lane
  commits into this checkout and pushes.
- The orchestrator chat writes lane UAT configurations and runs `uat.py up` and `cleanup` for lanes, with
  `source` set to the lane's clone; a lane deploys its own commits to its installation with `uat.py deploy`. A lane prompt MUST include: "Local deployments go only
  through `scripts/uat/uat.py` (see `scripts/uat/README.md`). Do not run the tm deployment steps by hand.
  Propose any change to `uat.py` to the orchestrator." Changes to `uat.py` are made on main by the
  orchestrator.
- Up to 3 lanes may each have one installation (about 1.4 GB each; `uat.py stop` frees the memory).

