## Context budget (Max, 13 October 2026)

Each turn re-sends the whole chat context, so cost is context size times turns. Every lane prompt restates these
two rules with their numbers; this file carries them for every session in this tree and in every hand-made lane
copy of it.

- Subagent rule. One task per subagent, with a written brief and a return limit. Keep a subagent under 100k
  context per turn and make it return a partial result before 200k. Pass `model` explicitly on every Agent call:
  `haiku` for mechanical work, `sonnet` for evidence gathering, `opus` only for judgment and package review. The
  Agent tool inherits the parent model when `model` is omitted.
- Worker tier by module (Max, 13 October 2026). Work on the Core module, the kernel, or restore and recovery code
  uses `opus` workers under the same caps. Exception confirmed by Max on 13 October 2026 for the Core lane
  `core-reads-2026-10-12` only: `opus` workers for Kind 2 items, `sonnet` workers for defects and reads, one git worktree
  per worker (at most three), waves by code area, partial return before 275k. Elsewhere
  `sonnet` workers implement a decided design from a written brief, with the item's Codex review behind every return;
  `opus` there for a fix whose cause is unknown, a change that touches kernel or transaction semantics across modules,
  and restore or recovery code. A Codex review that returns design-level findings on a `sonnet` item is the signal to
  change the tier.
- Core lane thresholds (Max, 13 October 2026, afternoon): the Core lane prepares for a compaction at 380,000 (guard
  hook at 380,000) and compacts automatically at about 430,000 (`autoCompactWindow` 463000). The other lanes keep
  280,000 until Max says otherwise.
- Parent rule. Check your own context at every boundary: before a new unit, after a package, before every
  subagent call (`get_usage` on session `self`). Above 280,000 tokens issue no new command or subagent, let
  running subagents finish and collect their returns, commit the unit if it is coherent or leave the edits on disk
  and write `state/RESUME.md` (files touched, intent, next step, pending decision), then stop and wait for Max to
  compact. After the compaction read `state/RESUME.md` and re-read only the files it names.
- Claude Code lanes carry `.claude/settings.local.json` (excluded from git): the `internal/tools/context-guard.py`
  PreToolUse hook refuses a subagent call above 280,000 tokens, and `autoCompactWindow` 383000 is insurance only
  (automatic compaction at about 350k is not the working threshold).
